From b2d42d02242016e0d270720cf19c384600014506 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Ushey <kevin@posit.co>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:05:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] add more r diagnostics for common errors (#18974)

* add more r diagnostics: repeated formals, duplicate args, bad assignment targets, bare return, trailing empty args, uninstalled packages

Addresses #9156, #9157.

* split news entry per diagnostic

* record primitives in the package index

Package exports that are primitives (rlang::is_null, magrittr::add) have no formals, and were indexed as closures taking no arguments, so calls to them were reported as having too many arguments.

* only flag bare return and require() as statements; respect lib.loc

A reference like quote(return) wants the function itself, and require() is an availability check whenever its result is used. A package loaded with lib.loc need not be on the library paths.

* leave require() alone when it is the value of a function or else branch
